<title>USA: FDA approves Perclose Prostar system.</title>
<headline>FDA approves Perclose Prostar system.</headline>
<dateline>MENLO PARK, Calif. 1997-04-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Perclose Inc said the Food and Drug Administration granted U.S. premarket approval for its Prostar 9F and 11F Percutaneous Vascular Surgery Systems.</p>
<p>The systems, which have been used in Europe and Japan for about two years, provide a minimally invasive surgical closure of arterial access sites following catheterization procedures such as balloon angioplasty, stenting and atherectomy.</p>
<p>Perclose said that it put a sales and marketing structure in place in anticipation of the approval.</p>
</text>
